## 4. Case Studies

### 4.1 Solar Project in California

**Project Name:** Solar Frontier Solar Farm  
**Location:** Riverside County, California  
**Capacity:** 150 MW  
**Completion Date:** June 2022  
**Developer:** First Solar, Inc.

The Solar Frontier project is a significant contributor to California's renewable energy goals, providing power to approximately 50,000 homes annually. The project utilizes advanced PV technology and integrates with the existing grid through a partnership with Southern California Edison.

### 4.2 Wind Farm in Texas

**Project Name:** Lone Star Wind Farm  
**Location:** West Texas  
**Capacity:** 300 MW  
**Completion Date:** March 2023  
**Developer:** NextEra Energy Resources

The Lone Star Wind Farm has become one of the largest wind projects in Texas, employing over 1,000 workers during construction. The project is expected to offset approximately 600,000 tons of CO2 emissions annually.

### 4.3 Hydro Project in Oregon

**Project Name:** Willamette River Hydroelectric Project  
**Location:** Marion County, Oregon  
**Capacity:** 50 MW  
**Completion Date:** December 2021  
**Developer:** Brookfield Renewable Partners

This hydro project utilizes run-of-the-river technology, minimizing environmental impacts while generating sustainable energy. The project has improved local water management while providing clean electricity to over 20,000 homes.

